Just thought I'd throw a word in without responding to anyone
in particular.

I guess the feature that labels the cursed bell as an 'abuse' is
the fact that it can generate lots of wraiths (i.e. wraith corpses),
leading to the really high HP/PP totals.  It seems that most of the
people who attack it bring that up.

Defenders of the feature say that if you are powerful enough to
deal with all the critters that show up, more power to you.

I propose a compromise for the cursed bell trick:
What if the cursed bell never produced wraiths?
Just have it produce all the liches and vampire lords
and other assorted dead things that it likes.
The people who like XP will get it -- they just
won't get huge numbers of wraith corpses to munch on.

Of course, I'm not entirely removing the ability to
kill wraiths on demand.  There are other ways to do
that. :)

Responses?  Flames?  Dev?

